# =============================================================================
# VAZIONIX — ENVIRONMENT
# =============================================================================
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; never commit real
# values. Everything marked SERVER ONLY is a secret. Everything prefixed
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is compiled into the browser bundle — putting a secret there
# publishes it.
#
# Every variable below is read by real code. Grep for it before deleting one.
# Variables the platform injects (NODE_ENV) are documented at the bottom and
# must NOT be set by hand.
#
# DEPLOYING ON ZOHO CATALYST (SLATE): create these same variables in the
# Catalyst console under the deployment's Configuration → Environment Variables
# (see CATALYST.md). Slate runs `npm run build`, so everything below must be
# present there too — including the SERVER ONLY secrets; they are injected as
# runtime env vars, not baked into any bundle.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. BOOTKEEP POSTGRESQL — the whole data layer
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by src/lib/supabase/* (client), src/server/supabase.ts (service-role),
# and the operator scripts in scripts/ (direct Postgres).
#
# The publishable key is safe in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ var; the service_role key is a
# server secret and must NEVER carry a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix or it ships to the
# browser bundle.
# SERVER ONLY — BootKeep internal PostgreSQL connection.
BOOTKEEP_DB_HOST=node3.botkeep.cloud
BOOTKEEP_DB_PORT=36224
BOOTKEEP_DB_NAME=postgres
BOOTKEEP_DB_USER=postgres
BOOTKEEP_DB_PASSWORD=
# Optional single-URL form; prefer the split variables above on BootKeep.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:<password>@node3.botkeep.cloud:36224/postgres
DATABASE_SSL=verify-none

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. ADSLAB — monetisation, tasks/offerwall, and the captcha
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by src/server/adslab.ts (secrets) and src/lib/adslab/config.ts (public).
#
# THE TWO KEYS ARE SERVER-ONLY AND MUST NEVER CARRY NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# The postback at /api/adslab/postback authenticates with a signature derived
# from them; either one in the browser bundle lets anyone forge a conversion and
# credit themselves. Verify with:
#   grep -r "ADSLAB_SECRET" .next/static   # must return nothing
ADSLAB_API_KEY=
ADSLAB_SECRET_KEY=

# Placement IDs are PUBLIC: they identify the slot, not the account, and appear
# in the SDK config on every page. Without them the SDK reads undefined
# placements and no impression can be attributed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSLAB_INT=
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSLAB_REW=
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSLAB_TASK=
#
# URLs to paste into AdsLab -> Website Settings (base only, no query params):
#   Postback URL         https://<your-domain>/api/adslab/postback
#   Captcha Postback URL https://<your-domain>/api/captcha/postback

# Shown in the footer, on the support page, and in the "email us" fallback when
# ticketing is unavailable. Defaults to support@vazionix.com / noreply@vazionix.com
# if unset, which will be wrong for your domain.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPPORT_EMAIL=support@vazionix.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_NOREPLY_EMAIL=noreply@vazionix.com

# Social links in the footer and the community page. An empty value hides the
# icon rather than rendering a dead link — leave Discord blank until you have a
# server.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_X=@vazionix
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_TELEGRAM=https://t.me/vazionix
NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCIAL_DISCORD=

# The public site URL: used for the sitemap, canonical URLs, the referral-link
# builder and OAuth redirect targets. Set it to the domain you actually serve
# on (Catalyst custom domain or the slate URL).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. CAPTCHA
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by src/lib/captcha/config.ts (client) and src/server/captcha.ts (server).
# Four providers are supported: adslab | hcaptcha | turnstile | recaptcha, plus
# `none`.
#
# HOW THE PIECES FIT
#   PROVIDER    picks the widget and the default verify endpoint.
#   SITE_KEY    public; renders the widget. No key means no widget, and
#               `captchaEnabled` goes false: gated actions run WITHOUT a captcha.
#   SCRIPT_URL  overrides the loader. Required for AdsLab, which issues a
#               per-account URL rather than a shared one.
#   SECRET_KEY  SERVER ONLY. Without it, and with a provider configured, every
#               gated claim fails closed with a 500 that names this variable —
#               deliberately, because the alternative is a faucet with a
#               decorative captcha.
#   VERIFY_URL  overrides the provider's verification endpoint. Only set it if
#               your provider gave you a different one.

# WORKED EXAMPLE — ADSLAB, the intended provider. Its captcha is a revenue
# product: a solve pays the publisher, so the anti-abuse control and the
# monetisation are the same widget. Take all four values from your AdsLab
# dashboard (Captcha → your zone), then uncomment:
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_CAPTCHA_PROVIDER=adslab
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_CAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=al_pub_9f2c1b7e4d
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_CAPTCHA_SCRIPT_URL=https://cdn.adslab.io/captcha/v1/loader.js?z=482913
#   CAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=al_sec_3e8a6d5c02b14f7a
#   CAPTCHA_VERIFY_URL=https://api.adslab.io/captcha/verify
#
# The site key and script URL above are shaped like real AdsLab values but are
# not real. Replace both.
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: leave PROVIDER unset (or `none`). Gated actions then run
# with no captcha, which is what you want on localhost and never want in
# production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CAPTCHA_PROVIDER=none
NEXT_PUBLIC_CAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_CAPTCHA_SCRIPT_URL=
# SERVER ONLY
CAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=
CAPTCHA_VERIFY_URL=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. ADS — client, safe to expose
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by src/lib/ads/config.ts. THESE ARE A BUILD-TIME FALLBACK, NOT THE NORMAL
# PATH. The normal path is Admin → Ads → Inventory, which writes the `ad_units`
# table and takes effect immediately with no deploy. The database wins over
# env, env wins over the static table in src/lib/ads/config.ts.
#
# Only six placements are wired to env, and on purpose: Next inlines
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* by literal lookup at build time, so `process.env[ComputedKey]`
# returns undefined in the browser. Each of these is a global overlay unit you
# might reasonably want frozen into a build before the console has data.
#
# TWO ACCEPTED FORMS PER VARIABLE
#   a bare URL           → treated as kind:'script' (kind:'url' for the
#                          shortlink direct link)
#   a JSON AdUnitConfig  → used as-is, so you can set network, cap and geo
#
# Bare URL:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_AD_GLOBAL_SOCIALBAR=//pl26481932.profitablecpmgate.com/aa/bb/cc/aabbcc.js
#
# JSON (single line, no trailing comma — a malformed value is ignored and the
# slot renders its placeholder, which is visible and therefore self-reporting):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_AD_GLOBAL_POPUNDER={"kind":"script","src":"//pl26481933.profitablecpmgate.com/dd/ee/ff.js","network":"Adsterra","capPerSession":1}
#
# WITHOUT THESE: nothing breaks. Unfilled slots render a dimension-labelled
# placeholder in development and blank in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AD_GLOBAL_SOCIALBAR=
NEXT_PUBLIC_AD_GLOBAL_POPUNDER=
NEXT_PUBLIC_AD_GLOBAL_INPAGEPUSH=
NEXT_PUBLIC_AD_GLOBAL_INTERSTITIAL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_AD_GLOBAL_ANCHOR=
# The monetised hop the shortlink engine sends users through. A URL, not a box.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AD_SHORTLINK_DIRECTLINK=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. PAYOUT RAILS — SERVER ONLY. These ARE secrets.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by src/server/payouts.ts. A rail is enabled by the presence of its key and
# by nothing else: an unconfigured rail REFUSES the send and leaves the
# withdrawal Pending with the tokens still locked, rather than pretending to have
# paid. Admin → Rail health shows which rails are configured, derived from these
# two variables.
#
# FaucetPay: dashboard → API → your API key. Scoped to send; the key can move
# your merchant balance, so treat it as a bearer credential for real money.
FAUCETPAY_API_KEY=

# CWallet: developer console → API keys. The endpoint is overridable because
# CWallet has changed its base path before and a redeploy to chase it is
# avoidable.
CWALLET_API_KEY=
CWALLET_API_URL=https://openapi.cwallet.com/v1/transfer

# There is deliberately no key for the Direct rail. Direct on-chain payouts are
# batched and broadcast from custody tooling; a signing key does not belong in a
# web process, and approving a Direct payout in the console only marks it
# Processing and records who approved it.


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. STAFF AND OPERATIONS — SERVER ONLY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by src/lib/admin/guard.ts. Staff rows in public.staff require mfa = true;
# a staff row without it is treated as not-staff, which is the correct default
# for a console that can move money.
#
# Set to `false` ONLY while enrolling your very first admin account (via
# scripts/grant-staff.mjs --mfa), then remove the line. Leaving it false
# permanently means a stolen staff password is a complete compromise.
# STAFF_REQUIRE_MFA=false


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. SET BY THE PLATFORM — DO NOT PUT THESE IN .env.local
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE_ENV   Next sets it (`development` for `next dev`, `production` for
#            `next build`). Read to decide whether cookies are `secure` and
#            whether ad placeholders render. Overriding it by hand breaks the
#            dev server.
#
# On Zoho Catalyst Slate, the platform injects its own runtime variables (for
# example ZC_SLATE_PORT when serving locally through `catalyst serve`); they are
# not read by application code.
#
# That is every `process.env` reference in src/. If you add one, add it here in
# the same commit.
